course: dictionary
lesson: 3795
title: A word for searching for food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A forager is a creature or a person that searches for food. It is a noun, so it names a thing. Its plural is foragers, which is what you call more than one.
explain: Read the context to check. «A honeybee forager dances a figure of eight on the comb.» The bee is the forager, and the rest of the sentence is about the comb and its dance, so a forager here must be a bee that collects food. Science lessons use it for bees that gather nectar and pollen.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «A honeybee that searches for food dances a figure of eight on the comb.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A forager is an animal that searches for food, such as a bee looking for nectar or a squirrel looking for nuts.
fact: A forager can also be a person who gathers wild food like berries, mushrooms and plants.
fact: «Hunter-gatherers» were foragers who lived by hunting animals and collecting wild plants before farming.
fact: A «forager bee» is a bee that collects nectar and pollen.
fact: Safety rule: never eat wild mushrooms or berries unless an expert adult says they are safe.
exercise: «A honeybee forager dances a figure of eight on the comb.» What is a forager in this sentence? | A dance move | A flower in the garden | A type of honeycomb cell | *A bee that collects nectar
exercise: Ellie picks blackberries in the hedge every autumn. What is Ellie? | A pilot | A baker | *A forager
exercise: Before farming began, people who hunted and gathered wild food were called what? | *Foragers | Farmers | Builders | Bakers
test: What is a safe rule for wild berries and mushrooms? | *Never eat them unless an expert adult says they are safe | Eat them when you are hungry | Share them with the dog | Eat only the red ones
test: What does a forager bee collect? | Stone | Wool | Mud | *Nectar and pollen
exam: Which word means an animal or person that searches for food? | Pilot | Baker | Gardener | *Forager
